   "cite": "asymmetric-tops",
   "prompt": "<p>The rotational partition function of $\\mathrm{NO_2}$ is 2238 at 300 K. Without the rotational temperatures, find it at 600 K.</p>",
   "answer": {
    "type": "number",
    "value": 6330,
    "generated_by": "ai",
    "hint": "In Equation 18.8.3 only $\\kT^3$ changes with temperature.",
    "solution": "<p>By Equation 18.8.3, $\\kqrot = (\\sqrt{\\pi}/\\sigma)\\sqrt{\\kT^3/\\kThetaA\\kThetaB\\kThetaC}$, so $\\kqrot$ grows as $\\kT^{3/2}$ and everything else cancels in the ratio: $\\kqrot(600\\ \\text{K}) = 2238 \\times (600/300)^{3/2} = 2238 \\times 2.828 = 6330$. A linear molecule's $\\kqrot$ grows only as $\\kT$, since it has two rotational degrees of freedom to the nonlinear molecule's three.</p>"
   }
  }
 ],
